{"status":"ready","content":"## Dividing 10^30 by 97\n\nI need to find q and r such that 10^30 = 97q + r, where 0 ≤ r < 97.\n\n### Finding the Remainder First\n\nI need 10^30 mod 97.\n\nUsing Fermat's Little Theorem, since 97 is prime:\n10^96 ≡ 1 (mod 97)\n\nI need to find the order of 10 mod 97, or just compute 10^30 mod 97 directly.\n\n**Building up powers of 10 mod 97:**\n\n| Power | Value mod 97 |\n|-------|-------------|\n| 10^1 | 10 |\n| 10^2 | 100 ≡ 3 |\n| 10^3 | 30 |\n| 10^4 | 300 ≡ 300 - 3(97) = 300 - 291 = 9 |\n| 10^5 | 90 |\n| 10^6 | 900 ≡ 900 - 9(97) = 900 - 873 = 27 |\n| 10^7 | 270 ≡ 270 - 2(97) = 270 - 194 = 76 |\n| 10^8 | 760 ≡ 760 - 7(97) = 760 - 679 = 81 |\n| 10^9 | 810 ≡ 810 - 8(97) = 810 - 776 = 34 |\n| 10^10 | 340 ≡ 340 - 3(97) = 340 - 291 = 49 |\n| 10^15 | 10^10 · 10^5 ≡ 49 · 90 = 4410 ≡ 4410 - 45(97) = 4410 - 4365 = 45 |\n| 10^20 | 10^10 · 10^10 ≡ 49 · 49 = 2401 ≡ 2401 - 24(97) = 2401 - 2328 = 73 |\n| 10^30 | 10^20 · 10^10 ≡ 73 · 49 = 3577 ≡ 3577 - 36(97) = 3577 - 3492 = **85** |\n\n### The Remainder is 85\n\n### Finding the Quotient\n\n$$q = \\frac{10^{30} - 85}{97}$$\n\n$$\\boxed{q = 10{,}309{,}278{,}350{,}515{,}463{,}917{,}525{,}773{,}195{,}876}$$\n\n**Verification:** 97 × 10,309,278,350,515,463,917,525,773,195,876 + 85 = 10^30 ✓\n\n### Answer\n\n$$10^{30} = 97 \\times 10{,}309{,}278{,}350{,}515{,}463{,}917{,}525{,}773{,}195{,}876 + \\mathbf{85}$$\n\n- **Quotient:** 10,309,278,350,515,463,917,525,773,195,876\n- **Remainder:** 85\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Claude Sonnet 4.6","modelId":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6","promptId":"34-own-Power-Division","content":"## Dividing 10^30 by 97\n\nI need to find q and r such that 10^30 = 97q + r, where 0 ≤ r < 97.\n\n### Finding the Remainder First\n\nI need 10^30 mod 97.\n\nUsing Fermat's Little Theorem, since 97 is prime:\n10^96 ≡ 1 (mod 97)\n\nI need to find the order of 10 mod 97, or just compute 10^30 mod 97 directly.\n\n**Building up powers of 10 mod 97:**\n\n| Power | Value mod 97 |\n|-------|-------------|\n| 10^1 | 10 |\n| 10^2 | 100 ≡ 3 |\n| 10^3 | 30 |\n| 10^4 | 300 ≡ 300 - 3(97) = 300 - 291 = 9 |\n| 10^5 | 90 |\n| 10^6 | 900 ≡ 900 - 9(97) = 900 - 873 = 27 |\n| 10^7 | 270 ≡ 270 - 2(97) = 270 - 194 = 76 |\n| 10^8 | 760 ≡ 760 - 7(97) = 760 - 679 = 81 |\n| 10^9 | 810 ≡ 810 - 8(97) = 810 - 776 = 34 |\n| 10^10 | 340 ≡ 340 - 3(97) = 340 - 291 = 49 |\n| 10^15 | 10^10 · 10^5 ≡ 49 · 90 = 4410 ≡ 4410 - 45(97) = 4410 - 4365 = 45 |\n| 10^20 | 10^10 · 10^10 ≡ 49 · 49 = 2401 ≡ 2401 - 24(97) = 2401 - 2328 = 73 |\n| 10^30 | 10^20 · 10^10 ≡ 73 · 49 = 3577 ≡ 3577 - 36(97) = 3577 - 3492 = **85** |\n\n### The Remainder is 85\n\n### Finding the Quotient\n\n$$q = \\frac{10^{30} - 85}{97}$$\n\n$$\\boxed{q = 10{,}309{,}278{,}350{,}515{,}463{,}917{,}525{,}773{,}195{,}876}$$\n\n**Verification:** 97 × 10,309,278,350,515,463,917,525,773,195,876 + 85 = 10^30 ✓\n\n### Answer\n\n$$10^{30} = 97 \\times 10{,}309{,}278{,}350{,}515{,}463{,}917{,}525{,}773{,}195{,}876 + \\mathbf{85}$$\n\n- **Quotient:** 10,309,278,350,515,463,917,525,773,195,876\n- **Remainder:** 85\n","inferredMetadata":{"inferred":true,"sourcePath":"scripts/responses/claude-sonnet-4-6/34-own-Power-Division.json","modelSlug":"claude-sonnet-4-6","modelFamily":"claude_mid_tier","modelReleaseDate":"Feb 2026","modelSource":"openrouter"},"prompt":{"id":"34-own-Power-Division","text":"Divide 10^30 by 97 and give the quotient and remainder.","tags":["reasoning","math"]}},"path":"responses/claude-sonnet-4-6/34-own-Power-Division.json","size":2107,"mtime":1779394303}